{
  "description": "What a pairing link must carry and which addresses it may name (ADR 0134). The Rust protocol crate and the Swift client both pass these cases. A case whose link starts with `SOYEHT-PAIR 1 ` is the text of a pairing QR code (ADR 0153): it is not a URL, and the same fields in the same rules make it valid or invalid. In every case `result` is valid, invalid, or old (the three-field link of an engine that does not prove itself). `weakEngineKeys` are the encodings of the eight points of small order (as hex): a link that carries one as its engine key is invalid, since such a key would sign for anyone. `nonCanonicalWeakEngineKeys` encode small-order points with y = p and y = p + 1, with and without the sign bit: a key whose y is not below p = 2^255 - 19 is refused whatever point it names. Whitespace around a link or QR text (blanks, tabs, newlines) is not part of it, and both parsers trim it before reading. A case marked `rustOnly` needs a point decompression, which the Rust client does and the Swift one does not: Swift skips it.",
